  "proof_summary": [
    "Consume the exact literal finite-data certificate returned by the actual all-order165 and inverse276 producers; C0/B are fixed inputs, not reselected from a different existential factory.",
    "The original source maps, degree n+1, displayed Taylor width delta, radial coordinate Y, height H and actual midpoint cell are retained. The numeric prescribed factory proves range geometry, Yprime<=(n+2)U and Hinv<=4U^2.",
    "The same retained physical profile gives k=(P0*sampleE0^A0)^(-1). Choose h=(4U^2)^(-1) and M=(n+2)U, all for the same physical component.",
    "The exact cost M^2/(h^2*k) is 16*(n+2)^2*U^6*P0*sampleE0^A0. Expanding U=B*(C0*sampleE0)^B produces a fixed coefficient and exponent before every component/sample/source.",
    "Only after the actual envelope has been normalized, the explicit hE0>=1 input permits coefficientEnvelope_pack to supply the single common K in the frozen principal cost. The reviewed normalization60 constructs this condition before the reference family is chosen."
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "The finite source certificate is an actual intermediate producer output; no final principal estimate, profile lower or final material bound is assumed. The next small adapter will apply the existing same-atlas principal criterion.",
    "Retained P/Gamma and original hT/hS/hN/hfield/K remain explicit. The raw optical/host inputs of the genuine finite-data producer are not projected from arbitrary Through03.",
    "The same enlargedMaterialData must be fixed before all source/family choices; this theorem does not change T or identify atlases built from different material witnesses.",
    "Static inspection only, no compiler/elaborator/CI, active source/index/ref/CP writes."
  ],
